Description: CVE-2026-8927 - url: detect proxy changes read from environment
 When curl reads a proxy from an environment variable, it failed to detect
 that the proxy had changed between requests on the same easy handle. Cached
 proxy Digest authentication state could be replayed against a different
 proxy than the one that originally produced the credentials (CWE-294,
 authentication bypass by capture-replay).
 .
 Track the last proxy string seen in UrlState::envproxy and, when the proxy
 differs from the previously remembered one, flush the cached proxy Digest
 state before re-using the connection.
 .
 Backported from upstream commit 5c225384b8d52c67ce8259c6e4203bc57aacb567
 (curl 8.21.0). Adapted for curl 8.14.1:
   * upstream curlx_free()/curlx_strdup()/curlx_safefree() helpers do not
     exist in 8.14.1 - replaced with free()/strdup()/Curl_safefree();
   * upstream re-anchored proxy logic into url_set_conn_proxies(); 8.14.1
     still keeps that logic inline in create_conn_helper_init_proxy(), so
     the detection block is placed there, immediately after parse_proxy()
     and before the local proxy string is freed;
   * conn->scheme was renamed/reorganised post-8.14.1 - the detection block
     does not touch conn->scheme/conn->handler so this rename does not
     affect the backport;
   * vauth/vauth.h is included to expose Curl_auth_digest_cleanup() (the
     existing http_digest.h does not pull it in transitively in 8.14.1);
   * the bundled regression test (test1647 / lib1647.c) targets the new
     first.h-based libtest framework (res_easy_setopt, libtest_arg2/3/4,
     test_lib1647, curl_mfprintf, start_test_timing) which does not exist
     in 8.14.1's libtest framework, so the test files are omitted from this
     backport. The core security fix is unchanged.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/5c225384b8d52c67ce8259c6e4203bc57aacb567
